order_type":"loop","frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":true,"uuid":"eceebad8-2b13-50f0-89a8-aa0bb984b2dc","relative_path":"elf_tree_platform.png","source":"data:image/png;base64,"}],"animations":[],"description":"# elf_tree_platform\n\nElf tree platform: a ring deck built round a great trunk (trunk section included, 53 u across), carried on curved brackets, with a rail and a spiral of steps up the trunk.\n\n- Footprint: 12 x 12 columns (192 x 192 units, 5.40 x 5.40 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -80..80, y 0..260, z -80..80 units.\n- Texture: 256 x 512, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering. Every visible face has its own texture region painted with its material at world position (seams line up across faces); identical faces share a region; construction and ruined pieces map into the region of the face they were cut from. No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: finished 48, construction_0 6, construction_33 14, construction_66 47, ruined 12 (0 rotated: roof slabs and a few leaning props).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- trunk: 56 x 260 x 56 centred at the origin\n- deck: 160 x 18 x 160 ring at y 160 (walkable)\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and scaffold, then walls rising inside scaffold, then full frame with roof rafters).\n- `ruined`: collapsed shell, broken walls, rubble, fallen roof (use with `_damaged.png`, or `_abandoned.png` for F7 abandoned buildings).\n- `elf_tree_platform_damaged.png`: damaged texture (scorch, holes, cracks) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n- `elf_tree_platform_abandoned.png`: abandoned look (damage plus moss, faded cloth, cold fires) = `abandoned_elf_tree_platform` together with the `ruined` set or the finished set.\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_platform_1` at (-56, 164, -56)\n- `slot_platform_2` at (56, 164, -56)\n- `slot_platform_3` at (-56, 164, 56)\n- `slot_platform_4` at (56, 164, 56)\n"}